    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 2.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe hine ofer ðæt feormige, forgylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.1"/> hine be his were oþþe he hine be ðam ladige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe hine ofor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.5"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> feormige, forgylde hine be his were oððe hine be ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.3"/> geladie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe hine ofer þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> feormige, forgeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.2"/> hine be his were oððe hine be ðam ladige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui cum postea firmabit, persoluat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.4"/> eum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.5-2"/> wera sua uel sic neget.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="128" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ se ðe hine ofer ðæt feormige, forgylde hine be his were oþþe he<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_2-2.attnote.fn.14"/> hine be ðam ladige.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wer ihn fernerhin beherbergt, bezahle ihn mit dessen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_2-2.lnote.de.1"/> Wergeld oder reinige sich [durch Eid] im Werthe dieses [Wergelds].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever harbours him after that, let him pay for him with his wergild or clear himself [by oath] to the value of that [wergild].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="129" ed="#attenborough"/>And he who harbours him after he has been declared an outlaw, shall pay for him to the amount of his<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_2-2.attnote.n.1"/> wergeld, or clear himself with an oath of equivalent value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who harbours him after that, is to pay for him with his wergild or to clear himself by an oath of that amount.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ofer <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ofer Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">soluat <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">soluat Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘seinem’ (des Begünstigers) falsch Q, Schmid. Richtig Brunner II 576 gemäss 20, 8. Wo Ine 30, wie hier Q, das Wergeld des Zahlers meint, sagt er <hi rend="italic">his agne</hi> <hi rend="italic">were</hi>. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 3; Eidesschwere 2 b. Später strafte Æthelstan dies strenger</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘his’ (the abettor's) Q, Schmid, wrongly. Correctly Brunner II 576, in accordance with 20, 8. Where Ine 30 means, as Q does here, the wergild of the payer, he says <hi rend="italic">his agne</hi> <hi rend="italic">were</hi>. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 3; Eidesschwere 2 b. Later Æthelstan punished this more severely</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">‘his’ refers to the outlaw.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_2-2.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><label>he</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">om. B, So.</seg></note>
      </div>
